{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "label": "fn_audit_row (generic audit trigger function)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Card ^ref-06 / R32: ONE trigger function for every table, so the audit shape cannot drift between tables and a table added by a later card cannot silently skip the audit. SECURITY DEFINER is correctness, not hardening \u2014 audit_log is deny-all with zero grants, so the insert must run as the owner (force row level security must never be turned on there). Reads actor and role straight from profiles rather than fn_current_role(), because that helper folds in is_active and goes null for a deactivated caller, and a deactivated session that somehow writes must still be logged. Branches on tg_op rather than CASE because referencing OLD in an INSERT trigger raises. row_id is RESOLVED, not assumed (^ref-62): `id` when it casts, otherwise the table's single-column uuid primary key, otherwise null \u2014 opening_costs (PK ledger_id) logged a null row_id and opening_balance_close (PK id boolean) made `'true'::uuid` take down the very insert it was auditing. business_date wins over event_date per ADR-007, and the reason column is coalesced across the schema's three spellings."}, {"id": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "label": "fn_audit_log_append_only", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TC-18: an audit trail that can be edited proves nothing. Unconditionally raises AUDIT_APPEND_ONLY so audit_log is insert-only and only the audit trigger inserts. Needs two trigger attachments because Postgres fires neither UPDATE/DELETE nor TRUNCATE events for the other \u2014 a before update-or-delete trigger alone would leave TRUNCATE free to empty the log."}, {"id": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_append_only", "label": "trg_audit_log_append_only (before update or delete on audit_log)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_no_truncate", "label": "trg_audit_log_no_truncate (before truncate on audit_log)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_attach_loop", "label": "trg_audit_<table> attach loop (blanket audit trigger over pg_tables)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DO block that creates or replaces an after insert/update/delete row trigger calling fn_audit_row() on every table in public except audit_log itself (which would recurse). Because this is a state file re-applied on every deploy, a table created by a later card is covered without anyone remembering to come back here \u2014 the failure mode migration 0005's RLS loop had."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_audit_log", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_profiles", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_costs", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260910000012_opening_balances_opening_balance_close", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_current_role_fn_current_role", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_audit_log", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_append_only", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_no_truncate", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_append_only", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_audit_log", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_no_truncate", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_audit_log", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_attach_loop", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "target": "supabase_functions_000_revoke_defaults_000_revoke_defaults", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.65, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "audit_trail_integrity_posture", "label": "Audit trail integrity: blanket capture, append-only guard, revoked defaults", "nodes": ["supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_row", "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_fn_audit_log_append_only", "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_append_only", "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_log_no_truncate", "supabase_functions_fn_audit_row_trg_audit_attach_loop", "supabase_functions_000_revoke_defaults_000_revoke_defaults"], "relation": "implement", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/functions/fn_audit_row.sql"}]}